    "body": "**Staff pay rates** sets each staff role's pay and how many officials each game needs. The Assigner and the pay report use these numbers.\n\n**Where:** **Setup → Tournament setup → Staff pay rates**.\n\n**To set roles and rates:**\n1. Under **Staff Roles & Pay Rates**, enter a **Rate** for each **Role** and pick **Per game** or **Per hour**.\n2. To add a role, type it in **New role name…** and click the add button. The remove button deletes a role.\n3. Click **Save Changes**.\n\n**Load my defaults** fills in your saved roles and rates. **Save as global defaults** saves the current ones for future tournaments (you may also be asked **Save these roles and rates as your default for future tournaments?** — choose **Yes, save globally** or **Dismiss**).\n\n**To set how many officials a game needs:**\n1. Under **Officials Per Game**, set the **Title for officials at this tournament** (for example Official, Referee or Umpire). It is used on schedules, assignments and notifications.\n2. Pick the **Standard officials per game**.\n3. For divisions that need a different number, click **Add Exception**, type text the division name contains (for example \"7v7\" or \"U8\") and pick **1 official**, **2 officials** or **3 officials**.\n4. Tick **Championship games use a different number of officials** and set **Officials per championship game** if finals need more.\n5. Click **Save Changes**.\n\n**Common problems:**\n- With no exceptions, every game uses the standard count."
