    "category": "Public pages",
    "keywords": "broadcast announcement banner message weather delay lightning alert followers push notification urgent announce post public page tell parents",
    "routes": [
      "/tournaments/*/broadcast",
      "/tournaments/*/communications"
    ],
    "audience": "staff",
    "body": "A broadcast is an announcement that shows in the banner on the public page, and can alert the phones following those teams.\n\n**Where:** **Live → Communications → Broadcast**. Directors can also use **Broadcast** on their home dashboard.\n\n**To send a broadcast:**\n1. Under **Audience**, pick who it is for: **Everyone**, **Division**, **Team**, **Coaches** or **Staff**. For a division or team, choose which one.\n2. Type the message, or start from one of the **Quick templates** (weather delay, play resumed, sideline reminder, championship photos).\n3. Turn on **Mark urgent** for anything people must see now.\n4. Leave **Alert followers’ phones** on to push it to phones following the teams it covers. **This goes to** shows who will hear it.\n5. Click **Send broadcast**.\n\n**To remove a broadcast:** find it under **Recent broadcasts** and click **Remove**.\n\n**Common problems:**\n- **Coaches** and **Staff** broadcasts are tagged on the public banner but do not alert phones, because coaches and staff are not followers.\n- Which staff roles can post is set in **Setup → Tournament setup → Broadcast permissions**. The director always can.\n- Phone alerts only reach people who followed a team on the public page and turned alerts on."
